Package: odrlITR
Type: Package
Title: Orthogonal Double Residual Learning for Individualized Treatment Rules
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jiaqi", "Tong", email = "jiaqi.tong@yale.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0005-8922-3386")),
    person("Fan", "Li", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Learns rules for choosing between two treatments from observed
    covariates, treatments, and outcomes using orthogonal double residual
    learning. Estimates treatment probabilities and mean outcomes with
    cross-fitted Super Learner or parametric models, or accepts predictions
    supplied by the user. Fits treatment rules with decision trees, affine
    rules, kernel or finite series methods, and neural networks. Provides
    formula and matrix interfaces, treatment recommendations for new data,
    and diagnostics for model selection and optimization.
